{:edb/db-before-t 2211 :edb/db-after-t 2212 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535524 50 #inst "2026-10-09T01:46:57.824Z" 13194139535524 true] [17592186100787 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353628 13194139535524 true] [17592186100787 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353639 13194139535524 true] [17592186100790 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353621 13194139535524 true] [17592186100790 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353635 13194139535524 true] [17592186101361 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535524 true] [17592186101361 1100 "Calculate the definite integral $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{2}(2x + 1)^{2}dx$." 13194139535524 false] [17592186101361 1100 "Calculate the definite integral ${\\int }_{1}^{2}{(2x+1)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139535524 true] [17592186101361 1145 "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =2x+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\ \\text{d}u & =2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u & =\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=2x+1.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 1 & 2 \\\\ u & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}{(2x+1)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{3}^{5}{u}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{5}{u}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{3}^{5}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}|}_{3}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{5}^{3}-{3}^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{125-27}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{98}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{49}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535524 true] [17592186353621 1017 #edb/ref 17592186353622 13194139535524 true] [17592186353621 1089 "q-113747" 13194139535524 true] [17592186353621 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535524 true] [17592186353621 1100 "Calculate the definite integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{3{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139535524 true] [17592186353621 1113 #uuid "1d07785f-